  "message": "Good question! They're part of my **available toolset** — the system I'm running in has a set of tools loaded for me at the start of each conversation. You can see them listed in my system reminders.\n\n**WebFetch** and **WebSearch** are in there as \"deferred tools\" — meaning they're available, but their full schemas aren't loaded until I explicitly request them (via **ToolSearch**). That's an efficiency thing: I load only what I need, when I need it.\n\nFor our finance team, I mostly use tools like **Read**, **Edit**, **Bash**, and **Write** to interact with the local codebase and run the analysis agents. But if you ever asked me to look something up on the web, I'd pull in the web tools then.\n\nDoes that make sense?",
